  <h1>NITP: Teaching LLMs to Model Meaning, Not Just Predict Tokens</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Standard NTP trains language models through discrete one-hot labels — a sparse signal that leaves hidden states free to collapse into a narrow, anisotropic cone. NITP adds a single auxiliary loss: predict the shallow-layer representation of the next token using cosine similarity. The result is richer geometry, +5.7% on MMLU-Pro for a 9B MoE model, and zero inference cost overhead.
  </p>
