<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ §01 -->
<section id="s-collapse" data-code="collapse">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Collapse Problem</div>
<h2>Hidden States Collapse Under Standard NTP</h2>
<p>
  Train an LLM with standard next-token prediction and something subtle goes wrong in its representation space. The hidden states — the rich intermediate vectors that encode everything the model "knows" about the context — gradually collapse into a narrow, anisotropic cone. By the end of training, tokens like "cat", "dog", "Paris", and "philosophy" may all be encoded as nearly the same direction in high-dimensional space, differing only in scale.
</p>
<p>
  Two metrics expose this collapse. <strong>Effective rank</strong> measures how many independent dimensions the representation actually uses (a value near <em>d</em> means diverse; near 1 means collapsed). <strong>Average cosine similarity</strong> between random token pairs measures how aligned, or "clumped", the representations are (near 0 means diverse; near 1 means all pointing the same direction). Under standard NTP, effective rank drops while cosine similarity rises — the hallmarks of anisotropic collapse.
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">representation-space.canvas — NTP vs NITP training</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">click a button to animate</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div style="display:flex;gap:.625rem;margin-bottom:.875rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
      <button id="btn-ntp" style="padding:.3rem .875rem;border-radius:5px;font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);cursor:pointer;border:1px solid rgba(237,100,100,.5);background:rgba(237,100,100,.1);color:#f87171;font-weight:600;transition:all .15s">▶ NTP Training</button>
      <button id="btn-nitp" style="padding:.3rem .875rem;border-radius:5px;font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);cursor:pointer;border:1px solid rgba(139,92,246,.5);background:rgba(139,92,246,.1);color:var(--purple-l);font-weight:600;transition:all .15s">▶ NITP Training</button>
